{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md'","aggregated_output":"# AccDSL project instructions\n\n## Mission entry point\n\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\n\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\n\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\n\n## Working rules\n\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\n- Follow the applicable policies under\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\n\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md && cat docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json && cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md && cat docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json && cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc'","aggregated_output":"# Core 0.1 debt source lowering, version 1\n\nThis executable profile supplements the protected Core 0 grammar and contract.\n`compile_source(text, bindings)` parses real source; `compile_program(Program,\nbindings)` accepts immutable typed declarations. Both bind names, check quantities\nand context, construct shared IR, and submit it to independent schema and semantic\nvalidation. Neither entrypoint reads the authored expected IR or expected results.\n\n## Repair execution audit\n\nThe approved P03 plan remains the implementation boundary. Inspection of the\ntimed-out attempt found two partial modules and no tests or deliverables. Its\nsuccessful example compile was insufficient: global constraints were dropped,\nrates were treated as dimensionless, and acceptance, package and domain checks\nwere incomplete. These are implementation failures, not evidence against the\nlanguage design. Repair them before accepting the slice.\n\nThe baseline is `borrowing.acc`, plus documented corresponding fields of the\nauthored IR, whose reconstruction claims are excluded. Independently constructed\ntyped programs and exact arithmetic checks supplement agreement between frontends.\nSchema validity is a prerequisite, not semantic acceptance. Negative IR cases must\nbe structurally valid before testing the intended semantic rejection. Stops are\nunexpected protected-input changes, missing dependencies, or failing mandatory\nchecks; failures trigger repair, never a passing report. No statistical, timing,\nusability, accounting-compliance or forecasting comparison is being run.\n\nProvenance of material choices: exact rationals, lexical rules and quantities come\nfrom `core-contract.md`; USD accounts and DebtMix fields come from the local\nDemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\nThe single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\nmultiple-source reconciliation is unsupported. Synthetic acceptance and admission\nrecords are supplied by the caller. Absence of reconstruction requires Unknown\nfeasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched cell, no witnesses\nand no solver results. Early diagnostics cover unit loss, silent constraint loss,\ninvented acceptance and copied package digests. A pass establishes deterministic\nengineering conformance only. Results are preserved in the two P03 deliverables.\n\nThe writable project files are the two versioned modules, checker, required test,\nthis profile, the versioned cases JSON and the two P03 deliverables. Existing\ngrammar/schema, authored fixtures, legacy validators, controllers, release-pinned\nfiles and preserved snapshots remain protected. Their current hashes are checked\nagainst phase-entry hashes where available, and before/after execution. Git is\nunavailable (existing marker is not a usable repository); no Git initialization.\nPython 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are existing dependencies. No\naccelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\nEquity roles respectively: the package report actually names these accounts.\nOther declaration names may vary. There may be multiple lets, Boolean constraints\nand conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nGlobal constraints constrain the parent family; alternative constraints stay in\ntheir respective branches and are not conjoined in the parent. No branch is\nselected or solved.\n\nBindings explicitly supply a digest-locked local package, synthetic reading and\nacceptance action, information/system cutoffs, opening balances, perimeter,\nsymbol admission, assumption periods/origins, and alternative authorship. Binding\nrecords remain separate from package definitions. Every acceptance must explicitly\nsay Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\nthe retained DemoDebt file and checks its fixed version, digest, exports and\napplicability. Paths escaping the repository and overrides are errors. The\npackage's registry examples and expected-result fields are not compiler inputs.\n\nDecimal tokens become Fraction directly; binary floats are rejected. Strings use\nJSON escapes, reject unpaired surrogates and normalize semantic strings to NFC.\nOriginal spelling and Unicode-code-point offsets remain in the separate source\nmap; typed locations identify constructors. LF, CRLF, comments and whitespace\npreserve semantics. Dates are Gregorian. All grammar words are reserved.\n\nExpressions include literals, shared references, `value(observation)`, unary minus,\n`not`, compatible addition/subtraction, numeric comparisons, typed equality and\nBoolean composition. Multiplication admits a dimensionless Real or Int factor;\ndivision requires a provably nonzero constant Real or Int denominator. Rates and\nYearFraction are dimensional; rate times money is rejected here (the general\n`simpleInterest` builtin is future work). Integer products remain integer; division\nof scalars returns Real. Addition and comparisons require equal types and compatible\ncontexts. `constant(rate)` is a scenario driver, with a constant, nonnegative annual\nrate. `external(string)` is admitted only for source/opening/report declarations.\nDebtMix principal must equal the accepted debt and opening liability, its fraction\nmust have proven bounds inside [0,1], and component rates must be constant and\nnonnegative. Interval arithmetic proves only conservative bounds; failure to prove\na bound rejects this profile and does not assert mathematical infeasibility.\n\n## Verification and remaining coverage\n\nRun `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p03.py' -v`, then\n`python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p03.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03`.\nThe checker returns nonzero for failed or skipped obligations, includes generated\nIR and binding projections, observations, diagnostics, hashes and runtime details,\nand writes only conformance.json and result.md under the declared output folder.\n\nThe semantic comparison retains IR values, contexts, locks, evidence, assumptions\nand all external bindings. It excludes frontend offsets and observation display\nspelling; those are separately preserved. The authored comparison uses debt value,\ncontext, contract types/fields, assumptions, endpoint conditions, scenario rate,\nopening balances and report policies. Exact one-year interest is checked as\nP * (alpha * fixed_rate + (1-alpha) * stress_rate), using evaluated generated\nfields. At alpha=1/0, P=100 and 5%/7% imply 5/7; 9% stress implies 5/9;\nP=200 implies 10/14. This calculation is not journal execution or forecasting.\n\nMC02/MC04 receive bounded context, evidence and assumption preservation checks;\nMC10 receives factual admission and explicit scenario-assumption checks; MC20\nreceives locked-package and override rejection checks; MC23 receives matched\ntyped/text tasks; MC24 receives parsing, binding, typing and semantic diagnostics.\nNone is wholly closed by this profile. G2, G12 and G15 remain open, as do all wider\nMC01–MC35 and G1–G18 obligations.\n\nUnsupported: general package loading, events, rules/overrides, postings, arbitrary\nreport mappings, records/arrays/field access, finite choices, nonlinear bound\nproofs, implicit conversions, multiple books/entities/observations, dimensions,\ncurrency/calendar variants, rounded or period observations, source conflicts and\nrevisions, cross-company mapping, extraction uncertainty, accounting elections,\nmeasurement estimates, behavior policies, future innovations and probability\nmeasures. Reconstruction, accounting execution, forecast validity, authoring\nsuperiority and human acceptance require separate evidence.\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"accdsl.p03.lowering-cases.v1\",\n  \"profile\": \"Core0.1 debt-lowering\",\n  \"source_cases\": [\n    {\"id\": \"borrowing_baseline\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"positive\"},\n    {\"id\": \"borrowing_crlf_comment\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"positive\", \"transform\": \"crlf_and_comment\"},\n    {\"id\": \"borrowing_let_arithmetic\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"positive\", \"transform\": \"let_and_compound_constraint\"},\n    {\"id\": \"borrowing_stress_09\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"positive\", \"transform\": \"stress_09\"},\n    {\"id\": \"borrowing_principal_200\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"positive\", \"transform\": \"principal_200\"},\n    {\"id\": \"missing_rate_unit\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"negative\", \"transform\": \"bare_rate\"},\n    {\"id\": \"unsupported_event\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"negative\", \"transform\": \"add_event\"},\n    {\"id\": \"reserved_identifier\", \"source\": \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\", \"kind\": \"negative\", \"transform\": \"reserved_name\"}\n  ],\n  \"typed_cases\": [\n    {\"id\": \"typed_baseline\", \"kind\": \"positive\", \"matches\": \"borrowing_baseline\"},\n    {\"id\": \"typed_principal_200\", \"kind\": \"positive\", \"matches\": \"borrowing_principal_200\"},\n    {\"id\": \"typed_missing_rate_unit\", \"kind\": \"negative\", \"diagnostic\": \"MissingRateUnit\"}\n  ],\n  \"schema_valid_negative_cases\": [\n    {\"id\": \"package_digest\", \"diagnostic\": \"PackageDigestMismatch\"},\n    {\"id\": \"wrong_reference_kind\", \"diagnostic\": \"ReferenceKind\"},\n    {\"id\": \"unbalanced_opening\", \"diagnostic\": \"UnbalancedState\"},\n    {\"id\": \"false_family_coverage\", \"diagnostic\": \"FalseCoverage\"}\n  ],\n  \"unsupported\": [\n    \"general package loading and overrides\",\n    \"events, rules, postings, journals and runtime execution\",\n    \"records, arrays, field selection and finite choices\",\n    \"multiple books/entities/observations, other currencies and calendars\",\n    \"cross-company mappings and broader uncertainty categories\",\n    \"reconstruction, feasibility proof, accounting validity and forecast validity\"\n  ]\n}\nmodule BorrowingExample version \"1\";\nuse DemoDebt version \"1\";\nsource note7 = external(\"synthetic-note-7\");\nentity Acme functional USD;\nbook Local entity Acme basis DemoDebt version \"1\";\naccount Cash : Asset book Local;\naccount Debt : Liability book Local;\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Local;\naccount Retained : Equity book Local;\nopening after2025 for Local from external(\"after-2025-close\");\nobservation debt : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 100 USD from note7;\nsymbol alpha : Real in [0, 1] because \"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\";\ncontract loans : DebtMix book Local {\n  principal = value(debt);\n  fixed_fraction = alpha;\n  fixed_rate = 0.05 per year;\n  initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\n}\nalternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\nalternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\nscenario rateShock { set market_rate = constant(0.07 per year); }\nreport statements for Local { mapping = external(\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\"); }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
